A complete virtual oilfield should be available before physical deployment.

VIRTUAL FIELD
      ↓
VIRTUAL WELLS
      ↓
VIRTUAL TELEMETRY
      ↓
RUST
      ↓
PYTHON
      ↓
KOTLIN

Simulation scenarios could include:

Production decline
Pump degradation
Pressure changes
Water breakthrough
Compressor failure
Pipeline restriction
Sensor failure
Communication loss
Facility bottlenecks

This creates a controlled environment for validating analytical models.

19. Digital Twin Feedback Loop

The long-term computational model is:

PHYSICAL FIELD
      ↓
OBSERVATION
      ↓
DIGITAL TWIN
      ↓
SIMULATION
      ↓
PREDICTION
      ↓
OBSERVATION
      ↓
MODEL UPDATE

The digital twin consequently becomes a continuously updated engineering hypothesis about the physical asset.

This is more significant than a conventional dashboard because it enables counterfactual computation:

What would happen if the operating conditions changed?

20. Energy Optimisation

PetroOS should model energy as an explicit operational variable.

Track:

Pump energy
Compressor energy
Artificial-lift energy
Processing energy
Water handling
Gas compression
Facility consumption

Then calculate:

ENERGY / BARREL
ENERGY / UNIT PRODUCTION
EQUIPMENT EFFICIENCY
FIELD ENERGY INTENSITY

The resulting system can evaluate production decisions against their energy consequences.

