23. Strategic Market Context

The broader direction of travel is already visible in the energy sector.

In August 2026, the U.S. Department of Energy announced funding aimed at digital technologies, smart-facility concepts and advanced analytics for upstream and midstream oil and natural gas, explicitly identifying continuous monitoring, AI-supported digital twins and infrastructure optimisation as areas for development.

This is significant because it suggests that the underlying technological transition is not merely theoretical: digitalisation, continuous monitoring and computational optimisation are increasingly being treated as strategic infrastructure capabilities within the energy sector.

